stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3.6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"217\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 7.852em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-mover><mjx-over style=\"padding-bottom: 0.18em; margin-bottom: -0.248em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-stretchy-h class=\"mjx-c2013\" style=\"width: 0.852em;\"><mjx